DISPOSITION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DLQInspectorPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable DLQInspectorPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
DLQInspectorDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web types/admin-diagnostics.ts 1:1, exposing
the list / global-audit / lazy-drawer-entry states plus the drawer selection, the replay-confirmation
target, and the replay-blocked banner. The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title +
subtitle, body never gated), the dismissible replay-blocked banner, the status header (3 stat cards +
the replay-disabled banner), and the two GlassPanels — the dead-letter entries table and the recent
replay-activity feed — each with an adaptive layout (columnar Grid on macOS/iPad, per-row cards on
iPhone) and full loading/empty/error/success states, using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no
hand-rolled glass). The entry inspector is an HIG sheet (KVList metadata + tabbed inner/raw payload
viewer with copy + a guarded Replay CTA); the replay confirmation is a stacked alert carrying the
interpolated `entry #{{id}}` message. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the
web key names; bytes/dateTime/base64-decode formatting is ported and harness-tested. Verified on BOTH
idioms by an isolated whole-Sources Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-check (macOS 0 + iOS 0 DLQ errors)
and an executed model harness (25/25). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to pre-existing,
out-of-scope errors in apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AuditPanel*.swift (forbidden to commit-fix),
